From 33ed631a43d239f21fd77148ad0b22ecb7f19194 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:59:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] PDP11 DUP: BOOT DUPn with a MOP bootstrap written for
 SIMH

The DUP11 has no boot logic of its own.  BOOT DUPn (PDP-11 only) copies
a position-independent MOP bootstrap (pdp11_dup_boot.mac, generated into
pdp11_dup_boot.h) to the top of the low 56 KB and starts it.  It uses
the board in DEC mode with its own CRC generation and checking, sends
MOP Request Program with device type 10 and the program type of the new
SET DUPn PROGRAM={SECONDARY|TERTIARY|SYSTEM} (default SECONDARY), loads
and starts the program with R1 = CSR.  HELP DUP gets a Booting topic.

